  "criteriaReviewed": [
    {
      "id": "cold_functional_capture",
      "finding": "Four sessions per role start with cold knowledge and no checkpoint injection. Each source-computed physical command is compared with the archived command before supplying its public return; both sides preserve the same commands and request order."
    },
    {
      "id": "selected_only_no_preview_acquisition",
      "finding": "Every retained capture point has previewPackingCalls == []; candidate proposal states form an exact four-field cold-state chain with only null entries added at the current epoch. All 18 captured checkpoints equal known cold or actual negative-proposal states. No learned events, model or controls appear."
    },
    {
      "id": "causal_owner_attribution",
      "finding": "Independent reconstruction from recorded node deltas found exactly the two Preview owner nodes as candidate-only IDs at all 58 points. All 36 candidate-only deltas match one retained attribution row each. Other node metadata and common delta identity/cause/order were checked; private node values were deliberately excluded as declared by the tool."
    },
    {
      "id": "no_permissive_count_allowance",
      "finding": "The consolidator requires every warmup and measured functional shape to equal its own frozen role form exactly. It then allows exactly four count paths, with both values checked against that form; no additive tolerance, wildcard subtree removal or arbitrary delta is accepted. Missing paths, extra keys, array length changes and other work differences fail. The implementation version identity is checked separately against the declared role version."
    },
    {
      "id": "program_and_owner_inventory",
      "finding": "Only preview_packing is added (55 to 56 owners), with no owner removed and no change in the 25 family-installed programs. Inventory scope is factory/family registration, not all programs installed during a live session."
    },
    {
      "id": "unchanged_core_tools",
      "finding": "All seven central timing/comparison/global-analysis tools were rehashed in candidate and Site95 baseline; they are byte-identical to each other and to the declaration. Cases and diagnostic comparison-policy bytes match the retained historical inputs."
    },
    {
      "id": "predeclared_global_statistic",
      "finding": "Global acceptance remains the pooled median of eight complete measured-session durations per case/version, independently for STCK and SMLP, strictly below +10%. The JS decimal-rational inequality and Python Decimal inequality preserve strictness at exactly 10%. Phase overruns are diagnostic; no cross-case compensation or added noise allowance is introduced."
    },
    {
      "id": "complete_sample_population",
      "finding": "The ABBA order A1/B1/B2/A2, 32 measured sessions and 400 actions, 8 warmups and 24 warmup actions remain fixed. All measured sessions and both cohorts must be present; only declared warmups are excluded, with no measured-outlier exclusion. Available p95 and phase results remain retained."
    },
    {
      "id": "provenance_closure",
      "finding": "Direct attribution inputs and capture/fixture links were rehashed, the canonical forms digest was independently recomputed, and all 302 baseline plus 306 candidate native source files match their captured manifests."
    }
